  ],
  "clinical_evidence": [
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "That's about the size of it. Eye pain, mostly. Nothing dramatic.",
      "start_timestamp": "00:16",
      "end_timestamp": "00:23",
      "supports": [
        "chief_complaint"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "So, eye pain since welding. Tell me how it started.",
      "start_timestamp": "00:24",
      "end_timestamp": "00:30",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "I was welding most of the afternoon on Tuesday. Or it might have been Wednesday, they've run into one another. Anyway, that night it began to feel gritty and sore.",
      "start_timestamp": "00:32",
      "end_timestamp": "00:46",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]",
        "clinical_uncertainties[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "So it came on that night, but you can't pin down whether it was Tuesday or Wednesday. That's fine, it isn't essential.",
      "start_timestamp": "00:48",
      "end_timestamp": "01:00",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_uncertainties[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Bright lights bother me. I wore sunglasses indoors yesterday, and felt daft.",
      "start_timestamp": "01:41",
      "end_timestamp": "01:48",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Moderate. I can work through it, but I wouldn't want to.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:00",
      "end_timestamp": "02:06",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Understood. Any loss of vision, or things going blurry or dark in the middle?",
      "start_timestamp": "02:07",
      "end_timestamp": "02:15",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "No, my sight's the same. Just sore.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:16",
      "end_timestamp": "02:20",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Good. So pain, bright lights make it worse, and your sight is unchanged. Do you wear glasses?",
      "start_timestamp": "02:21",
      "end_timestamp": "02:31",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.past_medical_history[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Short-sighted, since I was a teenager. I've got my glasses in my pocket.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:32",
      "end_timestamp": "02:40",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.past_medical_history[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "And does any eye trouble run in the family?",
      "start_timestamp": "02:42",
      "end_timestamp": "02:47",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.family_history[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "My mother had glaucoma. She lost a fair bit of her vision in the end.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:49",
      "end_timestamp": "02:58",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.family_history[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "I'm sorry to hear that, and thank you, it's worth knowing. What's your job, exactly?",
      "start_timestamp": "02:59",
      "end_timestamp": "03:08",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.social_history[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "I'm a welder at a boatyard. Twenty-two years now, so I should know better.",
      "start_timestamp": "03:10",
      "end_timestamp": "03:17",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.social_history[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Twenty-two years, so you know the risks well. Before I look at the eyes properly, any allergies I should know about?",
      "start_timestamp": "03:19",
      "end_timestamp": "03:31",
      "supports": [
        "allergies[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Yes, actually. I'm allergic to some kind of eye drops. I come up in a reaction, but I can't recall what it was. Years ago.",
      "start_timestamp": "03:33",
      "end_timestamp": "03:46",
      "supports": [
        "allergies[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Blood pressure is 132 over 84, pulse 70, temperature 36.7 degrees, and oxygen 99 percent.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:36",
      "end_timestamp": "04:45",
      "supports": [
        "vital_signs[0]",
        "vital_signs[1]",
        "vital_signs[2]",
        "vital_signs[3]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Both eyes look red, and the surface of both looks roughened, like a freshly sanded table top.",
      "start_timestamp": "05:30",
      "end_timestamp": "05:40",
      "supports": [
        "physical_examination[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "It's what I'd expect. A welder who lifted his visor, red eyes, a rough surface. That looks most like a flash burn, what we call arc eye.",
      "start_timestamp": "05:47",
      "end_timestamp": "06:03",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_assessment[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "It usually does, so no drops this time. I'm not prescribing anything. Cool damp cloth over closed eyes, rest, and sunglasses outdoors.",
      "start_timestamp": "06:14",
      "end_timestamp": "06:26",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_actions[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Two or three days off, and no welding at all until I've seen the eyes again.",
      "start_timestamp": "06:35",
      "end_timestamp": "06:43",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_actions[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "In your sunglasses, yes, but get a lift if someone can come. Do you want a note for your foreman?",
      "start_timestamp": "06:52",
      "end_timestamp": "07:04",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_actions[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "I'll write that today. I'd also like to see you again in three days, to check the surface has healed.",
      "start_timestamp": "07:12",
      "end_timestamp": "07:23",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_actions[1]",
        "clinical_actions[2]",
        "follow_up[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Good. And please, always visor down, even for a quick glance at a join.",
      "start_timestamp": "07:32",
      "end_timestamp": "07:39",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_actions[3]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "So to recap: rest, a cool cloth, sunglasses, and back here in three days. Ring the clinic if the pain gets sharply worse.",
      "start_timestamp": "07:45",
      "end_timestamp": "07:57",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_actions[4]"
      ]
    }
  ],
